# demo-video fake-agent cassette — Claude Code TUI, the intake side (Issue #2833)
#
# Format: <delayMs>|@input|@exec|@transcript|@hook <TAB> <payload>
#   - payload is expanded with `printf %b` (\e, \n, \t, \\)
#   - `{{INPUT}}` / `{{TASK}}` are the message CommandMate sent; `{{WORKTREE}}`
#     is --worktree
#   - the turn is two tool rows rather than one, because that is the beat the
#     cut is about: the half-formed thought the phone sent is written down as a
#     task contract FIRST (`Write(.commandmate/tasks/toggle-label.yaml)`, the
#     shape src/lib/contract reads), and only then handed to a second agent
#   - `@exec` REALLY runs `commandmate ask … --instance codex … --json` in the
#     pane (with CM_PORT from --port), so the product's send → wait → History
#     code path runs unchanged and only the LLMs are replaced: the codex pane is
#     codex-review.cast, and the reply `ask` prints is codex-review.jsonl's
#     final_answer read back out of History
#   - `@transcript` appends transcripts/claude-intake.jsonl to the file named by
#     --transcript, stamped at replay time, BEFORE the ready frame — the poller
#     reads the transcript the moment it judges the turn finished
#   - `@hook UserPromptSubmit` / `@hook Stop` report the turn's two ends to the
#     demo server the way Claude Code's own hooks do
#   - the reply frame is held 8 s after `Stop`, so the loop back to the idle
#     banner lands after the poller's 5 s capture cache has seen the reply
#
# Provenance: the frames reuse claude-delegate.cast's captures (real
# `tmux capture-pane` frames of a Claude Code session, sanitised) and keep its
# anchors verbatim:
#   running -> "esc to interrupt" (CLAUDE_INTERRUPT_HINT_PATTERN) and the
#              spinner+U+2026 line (CLAUDE_THINKING_PATTERN)
#   ready   -> a line starting with U+276F (CLAUDE_PROMPT_PATTERN) plus a
#              200-char U+2500 separator (CLAUDE_SEPARATOR_PATTERN)
# Stripping the ANSI or shortening the separator breaks real detection, so do
# not "tidy" this file.
#
# The running frame is on screen for the whole `@exec` (however long codex
# takes), and the `ask` output lands BELOW it for the instant before the next
# row repaints — keep the running anchors within the last 15 lines of the frame
# above the tool row, as here, so a capture taken in that instant still reads
# as running.

0	\e[2J\e[3J\e[H\e[38;5;246m✻ Welcome to \e[1mClaude Code\e[0m\e[38;5;246m · demo fixture\e[39m\n\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n\e[38;5;246m❯ \e[39m\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n  \e[38;5;246m⏸ manual mode on · ? for shortcuts · ← for agents\e[39m\n
@input	\e[2J\e[3J\e[H\e[38;5;246m❯\e[39m {{TASK}}\n\n\n\n\e[1m\e[38;5;220m✳\e[0m \e[38;5;220mCascading… \e[38;5;246m(3s · ↓0.6k tokens)\e[39m\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n\e[38;5;246m❯ \e[39m\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n  \e[38;5;246m⏸ manual mode on · esc to interrupt · ← for agents\e[39m\n
@hook	UserPromptSubmit
1600	\e[2J\e[3J\e[H\e[38;5;246m❯\e[39m {{TASK}}\n\n\e[38;5;114m⏺\e[39m Write(\e[1m.commandmate/tasks/toggle-label.yaml\e[0m)\n\e[38;5;246m  ⎿ 14 lines\e[39m\n\n\e[1m\e[38;5;220m✻\e[0m \e[38;5;220mFiling the task… \e[38;5;246m(6s · ↓1.1k tokens)\e[39m\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n\e[38;5;246m❯ \e[39m\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n  \e[38;5;246m⏸ manual mode on · esc to interrupt · ← for agents\e[39m\n
2200	\e[2J\e[3J\e[H\e[38;5;246m❯\e[39m {{TASK}}\n\n\e[38;5;114m⏺\e[39m Write(\e[1m.commandmate/tasks/toggle-label.yaml\e[0m)\n\e[38;5;246m  ⎿ 14 lines\e[39m\n\n\e[38;5;114m⏺\e[39m Bash(commandmate ask {{WORKTREE}} --instance codex "Give the header toggle a visible label. Keep it inside src/ and link the file in your reply." --json)\n\e[38;5;246m  ⎿ Waiting for codex…\e[39m\n\n\e[1m\e[38;5;220m✦\e[0m \e[38;5;220mDelegating… \e[38;5;246m(11s · ↓1.4k tokens)\e[39m\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n\e[38;5;246m❯ \e[39m\n\e[38;5;244m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\e[39m\n  \e[38;5;246m⏸ manual mode on · esc to interrupt · ← for agents\e[39m\n
@exec	commandmate ask {{WORKTREE}} --instance codex "Give the header toggle a visible label. Keep it inside src/ and link the file in your reply." --json
